<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4962" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμάρτ-ημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>failure, fault,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1261
			</span></i> (lyr.); freq. in 
				Att.
			 Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				3.3.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.65
			</span></i>, etc.; midway between <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδίκημα</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτύχημα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1135b18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1374b7
			</span></i>; <i>sinful action,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατόρθωμα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Zeno Stoic.
				1.54
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				5.3
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ περὶ τὴν τέχνην λεγόμενον ἁ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Plt.</u>
					296b
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Ap.</u>
				22d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴς τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					729e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τὸ σῶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					479a
				</span></i>
			.</div>
